<!--BlockML Documentation — copy A02 PageGroups into A03
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.task.A03_CopyPageGroups-->
<task:A03_CopyPageGroups xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:task="org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.task"
  xmlns:workflow="org.blockml.bml.transformer.workflow"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type">

  <baseType>
    workflow:InstructionTask
  </baseType>
  <is>
    A task that copies A02 PageGroups into A03
  </is>
  <documentation>
    A03 authoring task: create or update A03 PageGroups from BmlDocSet_A02
    page groups of the same name. Page membership is remapped onto A03
    pages or emptied; A03 groups with no A02 counterpart are deleted.

    - **Identity** — title, is, isNot, and documentation come from the
      matching A02 PageGroup
    - **Correspondence** — an A03 Page or PageGroup matches an A02 entry
      when the Block name is the same and only the sector package differs
    - **Pages** — empty if A03 has no pages yet; otherwise A03 counterparts
      only. A page with no A03 counterpart is omitted
    - **Links** — parentGroup, landingPage, and pages may name only A03
      Blocks; A02 or other-sector references are never kept
    - **Deletion** — an A03 PageGroup that is not in A02 is deleted
    - **Sources** — this task has no authoritativeSources
  </documentation>
  <properties>
    <instructions type="type:Text" override="true">
      <value>
        <![CDATA[
          All information for this task comes from the A02 PageGroups listed
          on BmlDocSet_A02 and from the A03 Pages that already exist. Do not
          read authoritativeSources on this task. Do not read BmlDocSetPlan
          as the source. Do not invent groups, titles, or page membership
          that A02 does not state. Do not create or edit Pages or
          pageMapping. Do not edit A02 PageGroups, BmlDocSet_A02, or any
          Block outside a03.

          1. Read the A02 groups
          Read org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.BmlDocSet_A02.
          Walk BmlDocSet_A02.pageGroups in A02 order. For each listed A02
          PageGroup, inspect title, is, isNot, documentation, parentGroup,
          landingPage, and pages. Those fields are the source. Do not invent
          a group that is not in BmlDocSet_A02.pageGroups.

          2. Resolve packages and correspondence
          The a03 subpackages data, page, and pagegroup
          (org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data,
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data.page,
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data.pagegroup) are created
          by A03_CopyDocSet if they do not already exist. This task does not
          create those packages.

          An A03 counterpart is the same Page or PageGroup in the A03
          package tree: the Block name is identical, and only the sector
          package changes (a02_structuring → a03_authoring). The remainder
          of the FQN after .data. is unchanged.

          PageGroup FQN =
          replace the prefix
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.pagegroup
          with org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data.pagegroup
          (for example
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.pagegroup.CoreIdeasPageGroup
          → org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data.pagegroup.CoreIdeasPageGroup).

          Page FQN =
          replace the prefix org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.page
          with org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data.page
          (for example
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.page.docs.CompositionBasics
          → org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data.page.docs.CompositionBasics).

          A page counterpart exists only when that A03 Page is already in
          the corpus. Confirm with inspect or scan; do not guess from the
          FQN alone. If no A03 Page with that name exists, omit the entry.
          Never fall back to the A02 FQN. Never invent a Page to complete
          a mapping.

          Write only under this a03 pagegroup package, never a pagegroup
          package outside a03 (a02 or any later sector). Do not write
          PageGroups outside a03.

          3. Decide how pages are filled
          Scan existing A03 pages under
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data.page (including
          descendants). Two situations:

          A. A03 has no Pages yet
          Every A03 PageGroup gets an empty pages composition. Omit
          landingPage. Do not create Pages to populate them.

          B. A03 already has Pages
          For each A02 pages entry, if an A03 counterpart exists, append
          that A03 Page (A02 order); otherwise skip it. Resolve landingPage
          the same way: use the A03 counterpart when it exists; omit
          landingPage when it does not.

          4. Write each A03 PageGroup from its A02 counterpart
          For each A02 PageGroup, resolve the A03 FQN (step 2). If that
          A03 group already exists, keep only the FQN / file path so the
          same Block is overwritten. If it does not exist, create it under
          the a03 pagegroup package.

          Example of the target shape:
          packages/bmldocs/blocks/org/blockml/bml/bmldocs/a03_authoring/data/pagegroup/CoreIdeasPageGroup.bml

          Each PageGroup must:
          - use baseType org.blockml.bml.docgen.core.PageGroup
          - use the A02 Block name as the Block name
          - set is from the A02 group, replacing a02 wording with a03
          - set isNot from the A02 group when the A02 group has isNot
          - set documentation from the A02 group, replacing any A02-task
            or a02-package sentences with: this group is the A03
            counterpart; pages / landingPage / parentGroup name only A03
            Blocks
          - override title from the A02 group title
          - set parentGroup to the A03 counterpart of the A02 parentGroup
            when the A02 group has a parent; omit parentGroup on the root
            (the A02 group that has no parentGroup)
          - fill pages per step 3
          - set landingPage only when step 3 B yields an A03 counterpart
          - omit every other aggregation
          - never list a Page or PageGroup outside a03 in pages,
            landingPage, parentGroup, or see-links

          parentGroup, when set, must be an A03 PageGroup written by this
          task. Write parents before children, or set parentGroup to the
          resolved A03 FQN even if that file is written later in the same
          run. Never keep an A02 parentGroup because the A03 counterpart
          is “not written yet”.

          5. Delete A03 PageGroups that are not in A02
          List every PageGroup under
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data.pagegroup (including
          descendants). If its Block name is not among the A02 groups
          from step 1, delete that A03 PageGroup file and remove it from
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.Library. Do not delete PageGroups
          outside a03.

          6. Register A03 PageGroups on BmlDocSet_A03
          Update org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data.BmlDocSet_A03
          when that DocSet exists. Put every A03 PageGroup written in
          this task into BmlDocSet_A03.pageGroups (TypeReferenceEntity
          links, A02 order). Remove any pageGroups entry that is not one
          of those A03 groups.

          Set BmlDocSet_A03.rootPageGroup from BmlDocSet_A02.rootPageGroup,
          remapped to the A03 counterpart. rootPageGroup, when set, must
          be one of the A03 groups in pageGroups. Omit rootPageGroup when
          A02 has none or the A03 counterpart is missing.

          BmlDocSet_A03.pageGroups and rootPageGroup may contain only a03
          PageGroups. If an existing slot entry is outside a03, remove it.
          Do not edit DocSets of other sectors. If BmlDocSet_A03 does not
          exist, skip this step — A03_CopyDocSet creates the DocSet.

          Export each A03 PageGroup written here from
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.Library if it is not already in the
          catalog. Do not remove catalog entries of other sectors.
        ]]>
      </value>
    </instructions>
  </properties>
</task:A03_CopyPageGroups>
